{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "id": "peer-network",
  "title": "Peer Network",
  "turns": [
    {
      "jobId": "d2e1380d-5287-4d23-a1a7-9ce92154c9de",
      "question": "Among declared industry peers, which stocks were the most central in the return-correlation network from December 2025 through March 12, 2026, and which pairs moved together most closely?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T18:36:14.559536Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T18:36:50.074647Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**BMY was the most central stock, followed by ABBV and PFE; GOOG–GOOGL had the closest positive return correlation.** These results cover **December 1, 2025–March 12, 2026**, in the declared same-industry peer network of 1,422 stocks and 13,248 links. [1]\n\n### Most central stocks\n\nCentrality is measured by PageRank—a network score, not a return or percentage.\n\n| Rank | Ticker | PageRank centrality |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | BMY | 0.008091 [1] |\n| 2 | ABBV | 0.007285 [1] |\n| 3 | PFE | 0.006446 [1] |\n\n### Pairs that moved together most closely\n\nThese are the five strongest **positive** daily-return correlations.\n\n| Rank | Pair | Correlation |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | GOOG–GOOGL | 0.9965 [1] |\n| 2 | BRK.A–BRK.B | 0.9891 [1] |\n| 3 | BF.A–BF.B | 0.9736 [1] |\n| 4 | BELFA–BELFB | 0.9458 [1] |\n| 5 | BATRA–BATRK | 0.9230 [1] |\n\nThe tool ranks links by **absolute** correlation. BYNO–CEPO also had a strong link, at **−0.9764**, but moved in opposite directions—not together. Centrality and correlation describe network relationships, not causation. [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — analyze market relationships — evidence `hermes-receipt:ab6641b74c607860f3425fe3967d6fdc951a687e5121e355085169f24a53998c`",
